From 5e63eacea80c3e5501602b2b9b4c35b9174897d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] SukiSU builtin-new: fix SUSFS detection and sucompat paths

Baseline: SukiSU-Ultra-builtin-new 5e63eacea80c3e5501602b2b9b4c35b9174897d3
Update: 2026-10-21, follow-up to the three-stage audit.

Changes:
- Add and register SUSFS extension ID 4 expected by the new manager; its live
  SUSFS status is still verified through the existing SUSFS status command.
- Accept /system/xbin/su as well as /system/bin/su in sucompat path hooks.
- Make the KPM stub path safe: no uninitialized buffer reads/copies, and an
  empty stub version reports -EOPNOTSUPP instead of falsely passing detection.
- Retain the Stage 2 Linux 5.4 fixes and Stage 3 exec/stat/faccessat bridge.

Validation:
- Applies cleanly to the exact builtin-new source archive identified above.
- git diff --check passed after application.
- This is not a claim of a full Linux 5.4/SM8350 kernel build; that source tree
  was not part of the uploaded files.
---

